  "run1": "Global DE optimum is the degenerate limit beta1->1, q->0 (all speeds ~0.995c, source 0.0015 d1 from observer). The note's point (0.667,0.143) is not a stationary point under these conventions: evaluated at phi=195.16 it gives RMS 4.20e-2, max 6.42e-2; a local polish from it slides to the beta1=0.999 bound.",
  "run3": "s runs to the 50 bound. With the other parameters fixed, s enters only as 1/s (intercept geometry is scale-free), so the s->inf limit is finite; during debugging an out-of-box Nelder-Mead polish reached s~1e12 with RMS 2.1425e-3 (beta1 0.5839, q 0.2037, mu 0.0724). No physical guard failed (2mu/r <= 0.0037 at s=50).",
